#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# min_by

#% text
# `min_by(xs, f)` gives the first element of `xs` with the smallest `f(x)`.

#% text
# `min_by(xs, f, n)` gives the `n` elements with the smallest keys, smallest first.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Keys are compared in the canonical order; equal keys keep the order of the elements.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
min_by(["aa", "b", "ccc"], string_length)
#% output
#= "b"

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The two smallest:

#% cell
min_by([-3, 2, 1, 3], abs, 2)
#% output
#= [1, 2]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `max_by`, `sort_by`, `take_smallest`
